@startuml
left to right direction
scale 0.8
skinparam dpi 120
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

actor "Dashboard / External Client" as client

rectangle "Node A" as nodeA {
  component "Runtime" as rtA
  component "TCP Server\n(protocol)" as tcpA
  component "Web API\n/api/introspection" as apiA
}

rectangle "Node B" as nodeB {
  component "Runtime" as rtB
  component "TCP Server\n(protocol)" as tcpB
  component "Web API\n/api/introspection" as apiB
}

rectangle "Node N" as nodeN {
  component "Runtime" as rtN
  component "TCP Server\n(protocol)" as tcpN
  component "Web API\n/api/introspection" as apiN
}

rtA --> tcpA : manages
rtA --> apiA : manages
rtB --> tcpB : manages
rtB --> apiB : manages
rtN --> tcpN : manages
rtN --> apiN : manages

tcpA <--> tcpB : TCP peer protocol\nJOIN/PEER_LIST/PING/PONG/\nGOSSIP_STATE/SENSOR_UPDATE/GET_DELTA
tcpB <--> tcpN : TCP peer protocol
tcpA <--> tcpN : TCP peer protocol

client --> apiA : HTTP GET /api/introspection*
client --> apiB : HTTP GET /api/introspection*

note bottom
Peer-to-peer traffic is best-effort over TCP.
Observer traffic is read-only and does not mutate distributed state.
end note

@enduml
